The question asks whether an interface can declare constants in PHP.

In PHP, interfaces can indeed declare constants. This has been the case since PHP 5. Interface constants are always public and can be accessed using the interface name followed by the constant name.

For example:
```php
interface MyInterface {
    const FOO = 'bar';
}
```

